Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:41:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip/prefill-decode-arms: landmine 3 narrowed -- not n_kv, not
 the buffer layout; the leading hypothesis is the physical KV cell indices

Three more arms on the 35B-A3B at full residency: LLAMA_KV_N_PAD_MIN=8192 (one n_kv bucket) and
ARMS_B_BATCH=512 (the decode context's reserve sized like the prefill context's) both leave the warm-rep
divergence unchanged.  What is left is the cell INDICES: v_cells is shared but v_heads is per-context, so a slot
sits in different cells on the two arms, and the tile-FA decode launcher splits the KV extent by index
(ggml_cuda_fattn_band_wmma_split / parallel_blocks).  T3's text point must compare two runs with the same cell
layout, or the pair needs one shared allocation cursor.
